 - Main documentation: ${getReadmePath()}
 - Additional docs: ${getDocsPath()}
 - Examples: ${getExamplesPath()} (extensions, custom tools, SDK)
-- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory
-- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)
-- Before implementing harness changes, read the relevant docs and examples in full, following related cross-references.`;
+- These paths are a source map for sessions whose active role and action space permit direct Pi inspection. This source map does not grant tool permission and does not override project, role, skill, system, developer, or user instructions.
+- If an active role or skill restricts this session to an action space such as orchestration, review, or planning, stay inside that action space. For example, an orchestrator that needs Pi docs, examples, source, or runtime inspection must dispatch a worker/subagent with that inspection task instead of directly reading files, running commands, fetching pages, or using other inspection tools.
+- For ordinary implementation/support sessions that are permitted to inspect Pi directly, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory.
+- For ordinary direct Pi work, relevant paths include: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)
+- Before implementing harness changes in a role that permits direct access, read the relevant docs and examples and follow related cross-references.`;
 	}
 
 	if (appendSystemPrompt) promptSections.addendum = appendSystemPrompt;
